        "quote": "4. **Never spawn baselines after with-skill runs.** Always launch baseline runs BEFORE or WITH with-skill runs in the same workflow turn. Spawning baselines after with-skill causes straggler waits and uneven timing data. [WHY: parallel execution ensures comparable conditions; baseline must match with-skill runtime environment. Evaluation-first workflows should run baselines first to establish ground truth before testing skill effectiveness. Exception: new skills on the quick eval path need no baseline.]"
      },
      "side_b": {
        "file": "SKILL.md",
        "lines": [
          206,
          206
        ],
        "quote": "| **Method** | Run 2-3 test cases manually (no subagent spawning); review outputs inline with the user; skip grading and benchmarking; **for improvements, still run baseline comparison; for new skills on the quick path, no baseline needed**; iterate on direct user feedback | Spawn parallel subagent runs with baselines; grade with assertions, aggregate benchmarks; structured inline review with markdown reports |"
      },
      "steps": [
        "Choose the quick evaluation path for a brand-new simple skill.",
        "Apply NEVER #4 as requiring baseline runs for every evaluation.",
        "Apply the quick-path table, which says no baseline is needed for a new skill."
      ],
      "why": "NEVER #4 requires baseline runs before or alongside with-skill runs for every evaluation, but the quick-path method allows a new skill to be evaluated without a baseline. For a brand-new simple skill on the quick path, the same evaluation therefore both requires baseline runs and permits omitting them."
    }
  ]
}

